  "term": "bilateral lesion",
  "definition": "A bilateral lesion is damage to or destruction of a structure on both the left and right sides of the nervous system. In this source, making a bilateral lesion in the parafacial respiratory group region prevented the usual increase in breathing rate linked to locomotion.",
